# Line-ending policy.
#
# Every builder in this repo writes artifacts with Python's text mode, which
# translates "\n" to "\r\n" on Windows. Without this file, a Windows
# contributor rebuilding a bundle can produce a whole-file diff containing no
# actual change, and — with core.autocrlf=false — can commit CRLF artifacts
# that then fail the `git diff --exit-code` drift gate on Linux CI.
#
# `eol=lf` pins LF in the working tree on every platform, and normalises on
# commit regardless of the contributor's core.autocrlf setting. Generated
# bundles stay byte-identical across macOS, Linux, and Windows.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated course artifacts. Byte-reproducibility is a stated requirement for
# these, so their line endings are not negotiable.
*.jsonl   text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.toml    text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf

# Never touch these.
*.pyc     binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.pdf     binary
